//! kat_vectors — known-answer vectors for the PORTABLE oracle path.
//!
//! Values were produced by an INDEPENDENT external oracle: CPython's
//! arbitrary-precision integers (`(a*b) % m` and `pow(a, e, m)`), which
//! share no code with this module and are numerically identical to
//! OpenSSL `BN_mod_mul` / `BN_mod_exp` (same mathematical function). This
//! is the same cross-language anchoring the `vdf` audit used (Python
//! `pow(5, 2**T, N)`). Moduli are random ODD integers of the stated width
//! (composite — the arbitrary-odd-modulus case that RSA/Paillier N and the
//! std.crypto.ff consumers exercise), NOT primes. All arrays are
//! little-endian u64 limbs. Generator seed 20260718; see SPEC.md.
//!
//! Each `SizeNNNN` struct: modulus `m` (odd), operands `a,b < m`, a
//! full-width exponent `e` (models a secret RSA-class exponent -> the
//! constant-time windowed path), and the reference results.

